<title>UK: T&amp;N gains on asbestos deal report.</title>
<headline>T&amp;N gains on asbestos deal report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in T&amp;N Plc rose in early trading on Monday after a Sunday Times report said the auto components group was close to completing a deal to cap its liability to U.S. claims on asbestos-related illnesses.</p>
<p>The stock was up 14-1/2p at 148 by 0824 GMT in volume of 178,000 shares.  </p>
<p>The Sunday Times said the deal could be completed within two weeks and should revitalise T&amp;N shares while also potentially increasing the chances of a takeover bid.</p>
<p>The paper said the T&amp;N deal would see it paying a 100 million stg premium to cover liabilities of more than 300 million to 400 million stg.  </p>
<p>It said that without the old asbestos liabilities, the company could be worth some 1.8 billion stg compared with its present market valuation of some 710 million.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
